WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:07.660
Lecture one's robot has two moves: a, one

2
00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:11.060
three, and b, two, minus one.

3
00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:15.434
Amounts between zero and one of each

4
00:00:15.545 --> 00:00:18.451
move fill a parallelogram

5
00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:22.810
with corners zero, a, b, and a plus b.

6
00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.860
What is its area?

7
00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:26.560
Pause and guess.

8
00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:33.730
Put a and b in the columns of a matrix.

9
00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:37.413
Its determinant is minus one minus six

10
00:00:37.413 --> 00:00:38.609
minus seven.

11
00:00:38.609 --> 00:00:42.660
The area is the size of that number: seven.

12
00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:43.385
Why?

13
00:00:43.385 --> 00:00:47.317
Read the three rules as facts about area.

14
00:00:47.317 --> 00:00:50.126
The unit square has area one.

15
00:00:50.126 --> 00:00:52.280
Stretch one side by t

16
00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:55.369
and the area is multiplied by t.

17
00:00:55.369 --> 00:00:58.366
Slide one side along the other

18
00:00:58.366 --> 00:01:02.017
like a stack of cards pushed sideways

19
00:01:02.017 --> 00:01:03.890
and the area stays.

20
00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:07.753
Those slides are the elimination steps.

21
00:01:07.843 --> 00:01:10.815
One slide turns the parallelogram

22
00:01:10.905 --> 00:01:13.877
into a rectangle: base root five

23
00:01:13.877 --> 00:01:16.399
height a little over three.

24
00:01:16.399 --> 00:01:17.480
Area seven.

25
00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:20.574
So what does the minus sign mean?

26
00:01:20.574 --> 00:01:22.860
Is the area somehow negative?

27
00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:24.475
Not at all.

28
00:01:24.475 --> 00:01:26.639
Take a small letter L.

29
00:01:26.639 --> 00:01:29.837
The robot's matrix sends it here

30
00:01:29.837 --> 00:01:33.036
seven times bigger, and mirrored

31
00:01:33.036 --> 00:01:35.952
as if seen in a looking glass.

32
00:01:35.952 --> 00:01:38.680
That flip is the minus sign.

33
00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:42.310
List the columns the other way, b then a

34
00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:45.110
and the determinant is plus seven

35
00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:47.030
the same parallelogram

36
00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:49.910
and now the L keeps its handedness.

37
00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:52.909
So the sign records orientation

38
00:01:52.991 --> 00:01:55.723
plus when the second column turns

39
00:01:55.806 --> 00:01:58.454
counterclockwise from the first

40
00:01:58.454 --> 00:02:01.020
minus when it turns clockwise.

41
00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:04.016
Signed areas add up nicely.

42
00:02:04.016 --> 00:02:07.237
A triangle is half a parallelogram

43
00:02:07.237 --> 00:02:09.205
the triangle zero, a

44
00:02:09.205 --> 00:02:11.800
b has area three and a half.

45
00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:13.435
For any polygon

46
00:02:13.516 --> 00:02:16.086
add half the determinant of each

47
00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:18.496
pair of neighbouring corners.

48
00:02:18.496 --> 00:02:20.906
That is the shoelace formula.

49
00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:22.995
Measured from the origin

50
00:02:22.995 --> 00:02:25.967
three triangles count plus, and one

51
00:02:25.967 --> 00:02:28.618
outside the field, counts minus.

52
00:02:28.618 --> 00:02:31.510
This four-sided field has area ten.

53
00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:35.671
What does a zero determinant look like?

54
00:02:35.671 --> 00:02:38.793
Start again from the unit square

55
00:02:38.793 --> 00:02:41.731
and send its sides to one, two

56
00:02:41.731 --> 00:02:44.485
and to one point four, three.

57
00:02:44.485 --> 00:02:48.250
The square becomes a thin parallelogram.

58
00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:52.251
Its area is three minus two point eight

59
00:02:52.251 --> 00:02:54.168
which is two tenths.

60
00:02:54.168 --> 00:02:56.085
Small, but not zero

61
00:02:56.085 --> 00:02:59.280
so the matrix can still be undone.

62
00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:03.109
Now push the second column the last bit

63
00:03:03.109 --> 00:03:06.762
to one and a half times the first column

64
00:03:06.762 --> 00:03:08.762
one and a half, three.

65
00:03:08.762 --> 00:03:11.371
Both columns lie on one line

66
00:03:11.371 --> 00:03:14.937
and the whole plane is squashed onto it.

67
00:03:14.937 --> 00:03:17.808
Every region loses all its area

68
00:03:17.808 --> 00:03:19.373
determinant zero.

69
00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:21.895
Nothing can unflatten a line

70
00:03:21.982 --> 00:03:23.722
back into the plane

71
00:03:23.722 --> 00:03:26.070
so the matrix is singular.

72
00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:30.045
Back to the plane, for the bigger statement

73
00:03:30.122 --> 00:03:32.668
a matrix multiplies every area by

74
00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:34.906
the size of its determinant.

75
00:03:34.906 --> 00:03:35.909
Take a disk.

76
00:03:35.909 --> 00:03:38.918
Under the matrix with columns b and a

77
00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:42.389
it becomes an ellipse, seven times the area

78
00:03:42.467 --> 00:03:44.318
every tiny square inside

79
00:03:44.395 --> 00:03:46.170
it was scaled by seven.

80
00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:49.142
A curved map is not one matrix.

81
00:03:49.142 --> 00:03:52.526
But near each point it is close to one

82
00:03:52.526 --> 00:03:55.656
the matrix of its first derivatives

83
00:03:55.656 --> 00:03:56.840
the Jacobian.

84
00:03:57.190 --> 00:04:00.345
Polar coordinates send r and theta to

85
00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:03.159
r cosine theta and r sine theta.

86
00:04:03.159 --> 00:04:05.803
Its Jacobian determinant is r.

87
00:04:05.803 --> 00:04:08.446
A small patch near the centre

88
00:04:08.446 --> 00:04:12.113
and the same steps of r and theta far out

89
00:04:12.113 --> 00:04:15.950
the far patch is bigger, in proportion to r.

90
00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:20.260
Add up the patches, r delta r delta theta

91
00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:23.560
over the whole disk of radius two

92
00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:27.426
and the sum is four pi, as it should be.

93
00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:30.443
That is the change of variables

94
00:04:30.537 --> 00:04:32.140
rule of calculus.

95
00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:34.988
Machine learning meets this

96
00:04:35.072 --> 00:04:36.752
through probability.

97
00:04:36.752 --> 00:04:40.112
A density is probability per unit area.

98
00:04:40.112 --> 00:04:42.464
Push data through a matrix

99
00:04:42.464 --> 00:04:45.908
a patch's area grows by the determinant

100
00:04:45.908 --> 00:04:49.268
but the probability inside it does not.

101
00:04:49.268 --> 00:04:52.040
So the density is divided by it.

102
00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:55.264
Send two hundred thousand random points

103
00:04:55.337 --> 00:04:57.327
through the robot's matrix.

104
00:04:57.401 --> 00:04:59.980
The share landing in a small square

105
00:05:00.053 --> 00:05:02.116
is point zero zero five one

106
00:05:02.116 --> 00:05:04.990
the formula says point zero zero five.

107
00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:08.722
In logs, the log-determinant is subtracted.

108
00:05:08.722 --> 00:05:12.183
Normalizing flows are models built on this

109
00:05:12.183 --> 00:05:14.306
with triangular Jacobians

110
00:05:14.385 --> 00:05:16.745
so the log-determinant is just

111
00:05:16.823 --> 00:05:18.790
a sum along the diagonal.

112
00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:20.756
And compute it as a log

113
00:05:20.835 --> 00:05:23.902
take one half times the identity in one

114
00:05:23.981 --> 00:05:26.498
thousand two hundred dimensions

115
00:05:26.576 --> 00:05:29.093
its determinant is so small that

116
00:05:29.172 --> 00:05:31.060
the computer shows zero

117
00:05:31.138 --> 00:05:33.812
but its log is minus eight hundred

118
00:05:33.891 --> 00:05:35.700
thirty-one point eight.

119
00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:39.471
So: the determinant is a signed area

120
00:05:39.557 --> 00:05:42.316
and the factor by which a matrix

121
00:05:42.402 --> 00:05:44.127
scales every region.

122
00:05:44.127 --> 00:05:46.800
The Jacobian makes that local.

123
00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:48.206
Next unit

124
00:05:48.206 --> 00:05:51.591
directions that a matrix only stretches

125
00:05:51.591 --> 00:05:53.407
without turning them.

126
00:05:53.407 --> 00:05:55.389
Those are eigenvectors

127
00:05:55.471 --> 00:05:57.948
and the product of the stretch

128
00:05:58.031 --> 00:06:00.260
factors is the determinant.
